{"repositoryId":351249217,"availability":"available","full":"JavaFXpert/quantum-music-playground","name":"quantum-music-playground","description":"New version","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":64,"forks":11,"created":"2021-03-24T23:14:47Z","updated":"2023-10-11T19:41:32Z","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://twitter.com/JavaFXpert","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T08:21:57.257Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T08:21:57.257Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T08:21:57.257Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T08:21:57.257Z","stars":64,"forks":11}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Playground for composing music using quantum states. Implemented as a Max for Live device in Ableton Live 11, and includes a MicroQiskit quantum simulator. Free, open source, Apache 2.0 licensed. Developed by James L. Weaver, @JavaFXpert on Twitter.","Here is a video presentation of Quantum Music Playground during the Quantum Sounds Symposium at the Institute of Photonic Sciences (ICFO) in Barcelona on June 7, 2023.","Here is a Quantum Music Playground presentation video given at IBM Quantum Educators Summit on 4-Aug-2021."],"features":["The Ableton Live set from which many of the examples in this tutorial were taken may be downloaded from the sets folder of the Quantum Music Playground repository. Please open this set in Ableton Live 11.","It is necessary to download the Quantum Music Playground v0.95 device from the releases folder of the Quantum Music Playground repository and drag it into its own empty MIDI track (by convention in the leftmost track,…","Because there are no gates on wire q0, the drum may only play on basis states whose 0 (least significant) position contains 0.","Because there are no gates on wire q1, the drum may only play on basis states whose 1 position contains 0.","Because there is an H gate on wire q2, the drum may play on basis states whose 2 position contains either 0 or 1. This is because the H gate puts the wire into a combination of 0 and 1."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JavaFXpert/quantum-music-playground/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"634068cbbd3b8544b0df41569c4e1f554b7ed062e404383adc0b8ae9d7861b76","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T08:21:57.407Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T08:21:57.407Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Playground for composing music using quantum states. Implemented as a Max for Live device in Ableton Live 11, and includes a MicroQiskit quantum simulator. Free, open source, Apache 2.0 licensed. Developed by James L. Weaver, @JavaFXpert on Twitter.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JavaFXpert/quantum-music-playground/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"634068cbbd3b8544b0df41569c4e1f554b7ed062e404383adc0b8ae9d7861b76","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JavaFXpert/quantum-music-playground/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-16T08:21:57.408Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2023-10-11T19:41:32Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JavaFXpert/quantum-music-playground/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-16T08:21:57.412Z","hash":"634068cbbd3b8544b0df41569c4e1f554b7ed062e404383adc0b8ae9d7861b76","originalBytes":40787,"storedBytes":40787,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["quantum","music","gate","playground","basis","following","states","twinkle","gates","clip","screenshot","images","v095","phase","which","musical","drum","notes","may","bass","control","note","one","image","play","wire","circuit","whose","each","midi","column","example","out","contains","sequence","here","pitches","played","position","now","state","button","labeled","live","qmp","some","time","ableton","device","grid","playing","when","beat","bit","using","video","clips","hats","left","part","selecting","modifiers","only","pattern","qmp.png","slider","there","used","instruments","number","right","shows","toggle","because","another","bottom